    "kind": "colony_width",
    "note": "WoRMS (Veron 1986, Richmond 1997) describes Montipora digitata as digitate colonies forming mounds over 40 cm across and M. capricornis as thin plates or whorls; wild plating colonies exceed a metre. Aquarium colonies are typically 5 to 20 cm. 15 cm is the width of a mature display colony including its small rock base and the extended polyps at the margin. Corallites are 0.5 to 1.5 mm (Coral Trait Database: M. digitata corallite width 0.8 to 0.9 mm); the LOD1 polyps are 1.8 to 2.6 mm tubes of which 1.4 to 2.2 mm stand above the surface."
